From 52412cbf14afcbb2a90a60723136aaab7fd23300 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:43:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-116: the snapSpacing setting -- the spacing
 snaplines' distance (0.116.0)

Dragging, a component snaps at a fixed distance from its neighbour on the same
row / column (the spacing snaplines, WPF's snapping). That distance was fixed at
8 px (BCB6's grid step). New setting ht9045Designer.snapSpacing = px (8 by
default, 0 = no spacing snap, 64 at most); a change reaches the open designers
at once. With it the four settings WPF's XAML Designer options have that were
open here (zoom by, default zoom, default view, snapping) are done.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 192, panels, real VS Code 159):
probe (12: lands 12 px from the neighbour; 0: stays where let go, 10 px); smoke
(init says 8; 12 / 500 -> 64 / nonsense -> 8 / removed -> 8, each told at once).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
